Task 2 is finished: --output-format stream-json now writes -o, so #1219 closes when this is pushed. The previous attempt committed the work before it was interrupted (2b7b4a7d), and this pass only checked it and dealt with one leftover.

What changed:
• The bug: both stream-json paths (-p and piped input) returned before the only code that writes the -o file. So -o out.txt created nothing, printed nothing, and exited 0.
• The fix: every output format now goes through the same output-file check, write_output_for_outcome in src/main.rs, using the same failure rule as the other modes.
  • A successful run writes the answer to the file and prints "wrote response to" or "replaced" on stderr.
  • A failed or interrupted run leaves the file untouched (or doesn't create it) and says it "was not written".
  • stdout is still pure NDJSON.
• Ctrl+C: the stream-json loop caught Ctrl+C itself without marking the run as interrupted, so a partial reply would have replaced the file and exited 0. It now marks it, keeps the file and exits 130, like plain -p (a one-line change in src/prompt.rs).
• Tests: six new rows in tests/output_failed_run.rs cover success with and without an existing file, a refusal, an HTTP 400, Ctrl+C, and piped input. Each stdout line is checked as JSON in the success, refusal and piped-input rows.
• Recall control: I disabled the new write with a NEUTERED marker and checked the marker count before running. The five -p stream-json rows failed by name; after restoring, all passed. A second control did the same for the piped call site. Both results are on #1219.
• Docs: the --output section of docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md now says the rules apply to stream-json too.

Checks: this pass ran cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings, cargo build and the full cargo test; all passed, with no NEUTERED markers left and a clean working tree. Nothing new to commit.

Still open: if stream-json is killed with SIGTERM, SIGHUP or SIGQUIT, the process ends at once (the signal handler at prompt.rs:1107 only runs on the text path). The file is left alone, which is correct, but stderr doesn't say so. I found this by reading the code and haven't run it. Since #1219 closes on push, I added it to the open #1221 (the same problem for --output-format json) and widened that ticket to cover every output format.
